# WN22-DC-000405: Windows Server 2022 must be configured for certificate-based authentication for domain controllers.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000405-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must be configured for certificate-based authentication for domain controllers.`
    description `Active Directory domain services elevation of privilege vulnerability could allow a user rights to the system, such as administrative and other high-level capabilities.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium,ksi-afr-ads,ksi-iam-apm,ksi-iam-elp,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-AFR-ADS,KSI:KSI-IAM-APM,KSI:KSI-IAM-ELP,KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:AC-3`
    control_objective `KSI-AFR-ADS,KSI-IAM-APM,KSI-IAM-ELP,KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the registry value. Registry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE Registry Path: SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Kdc Value Name: StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement Value Type: REG_DWORD Value: 0x00000001 (1) or 0x00000002 (2)`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_AFR_ADS `Windows Server implements KSI-AFR-ADS by setting registry value 'StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINESYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Kdc' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_APM `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-APM by setting registry value 'StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINESYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Kdc' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_ELP `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-ELP by setting registry value 'StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINESYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Kdc' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by setting registry value 'StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINESYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Kdc' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_AC_3 `Windows Server implements AC-3 by setting registry value 'StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINESYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Kdc' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Kdc`
        name `StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
